# Test: The shipped OSPF decoder selects its file operand and accepts explicit stdin
# VALIDATES: spec-web-cli-config-one-off-defects AC-1 through the registered root
# command. Unit subprocesses call cmdDecode directly and cannot prove that root
# dispatch preserves the new input operand in the built ze executable.
# PREVENTS: root dispatch dropping a capture path or refusing the dash input.

tmpfs=ospf.hex:terminator=EOF_OSPF
020100300a00000100000000949300000000000000000000ffffff00000a4201000000280a0000010a0000020a000003
EOF_OSPF
stdin=wrong:terminator=EOF_WRONG
invalid stdin must not replace the file
EOF_WRONG
stdin=packet:hex=020100300a00000100000000949300000000000000000000ffffff00000a4201000000280a0000010a0000020a000003

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze ospf decode ospf.hex:stdin=wrong
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="type":"hello"
expect=stdout:contains="router-id":"10.0.0.1"

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze ospf decode -:stdin=packet
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="type":"hello"
expect=stdout:contains="router-id":"10.0.0.1"
